# rule.always.yield-the-output-not-the-archaeology

> a yield is the output, never the archaeology.

state the answer. a path worth a record goes in a peer dir, cited by path: `$route/appendix/` (evidence under a decision in the yield) · `$route/archive/` (ideas rejected).

in the yield: contract/outcome, decision, one line of reason, fulcrum row (what settled, by whom), caveat a reader must act on. not: drafts, reversals, full argument, blow-by-blow, review-process commentary.

declare each claim once. before: *"is this the answer, or the story of the answer?"* after: grep each decision's central term; more than 2-3 hits = a retold story.

tells: table rows that are drafts · "an earlier draft" · a section on why a prior version was wrong · one fulcrum cited four times · a yield that grew on a round where no decision changed.

caveats: a reversal a reader must ACT on stays · terse is not thin · `archive/` is not deletion · an appendix must be cited.
